userStories.description:
**Goal** — Implement Git-index-safe temporary base configuration pinning and current-HEAD restoration.

**Motivation** — `runBotFix` prepares its checkout with `pinBaseFiles: false` (`src/bot/fix-run.ts`), so the fix agent loads the PR head's `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `.claude/` settings and hooks, `.mcp.json` and `.nax/rules`.

**Approach** — **Session-scoped base pin (S5).** A new module `src/bot/session-pin.ts` pins the base agent configuration into a worktree for the length of one agent session and puts the head's back afterwards (skeleton below). It reads the pinned files of `HEAD` and of the base with `ls-tree`, removes the head copies, checks out the base copies, resets the index for those paths to `HEAD`, records each base-only file as intent-to-add (`git add -N`), and marks every pinned file present in the index (head files and the intent-to-add base-only files) `skip-worktree`, so the agent's `git add -A`, `git status` and `git commit -a` leave them all out (checked with git 2.50.1). Restore clears `skip-worktree`, resets the index for those paths to `HEAD` (which drops the intent-to-add entries), removes every pinned path and checks the pinned files of the then-current `HEAD` out again, so an agent commit that changed a pinned file stays in `HEAD` and is refused as `protected` by `checkStep`. A pinned path whose parent inside the worktree is a symlink or a regular file is skipped with a warning, both when pinning and again immediately before each removal at restore (the agent may have swapped a directory for a link during the session). Pathspec arguments to `checkout`, `reset` and `add -N` carry the `:(literal)` magic prefix, so a file name with glob characters matches only itself; `update-index` takes plain paths. Every git call goes through `botGit`.

**Scope** — In: core pin/restore Git mechanics, SessionPin and _sessionPinDeps, NaxError failure mapping and real-repo/index tests. Out: the parent-path safety sentence above and basePinScope wrapper are implemented by downstream US-004; fix/repair context and prompts belong to US-005, and protected-path enforcement belongs to US-002. Do not reuse the review's pinInstructions: it stages base copies and dirties fix safety checks. A per-worktree info/exclude is not read by git and is not a substitute for intent-to-add plus skip-worktree. An agent that deliberately clears `skip-worktree` and commits a pinned file gets its fix refused as `protected`; the pin does not try to prevent that. An uncommitted agent edit to a pinned file is discarded when the head's copy is restored; the fix proceeds without it. A fix process killed mid-session leaves its throwaway worktree pinned (skip-worktree set); no recovery path reuses that worktree's index, and the saved fix keeps only the commit.

**Interface** —
```ts
import { lstat, rm } from "node:fs/promises";
import { botGit } from "./git";
import { isPinnedPath } from "./path-policy";

export const _sessionPinDeps = {
  runGit: botGit,
  rm: (path: string) => rm(path, { recursive: true, force: true }),
  lstat,
};

export interface SessionPin {
  /** Repo-relative pinned files touched: head copies removed, base copies written. */
  readonly paths: readonly string[];
  /** Put the head's (current HEAD's) pinned files back; clears skip-worktree. */
  restore(): Promise<void>;
}

export async function pinBaseForSession(worktree: string, baseSha: string): Promise<SessionPin>;
```

`ls-tree -r HEAD and <baseSha>, keep isPinnedPath files, drop any under a linked or non-directory parent (warn), rm head copies, checkout <baseSha> -- <base files>, reset -q HEAD -- <all>, add -N -- <base-only files>, update-index --skip-worktree -- <head files + base-only files>`. Parent checks are the US-004 extension; the remaining algorithm is this story. `checkout`, `reset` and `add -N` pathspecs carry `:(literal)`; `update-index` takes plain paths (it rejects the magic prefix); every `ls-tree` is `-r --name-only -z`. Throws BOT_SESSION_PIN_FAILED on a git failure.

`restore()` runs `update-index --no-skip-worktree -- <head files + base-only files>` (plain paths), `reset -q HEAD -- <all>` (`:(literal)` pathspecs), removes every path in `paths` whose parents are still real directories (re-checked with `lstat` right before each removal; a linked or non-directory parent is skipped with the same warning), lists the pinned files of the current `HEAD` with `ls-tree -r` and checks them out from `HEAD`; it throws `BOT_SESSION_RESTORE_FAILED` on a git failure. With no pinned file at either side, `pinBaseForSession` runs only the two `ls-tree` calls. The lstat safety portion is delivered in US-004.

A git call in pinBaseForSession failing must produce NaxError BOT_SESSION_PIN_FAILED with stage bot-fix; a restore git failure produces BOT_SESSION_RESTORE_FAILED. Fixture for every integration AC: a real repo whose base commit has CLAUDE.md reading base and .mcp.json reading base-mcp, and whose checked-out head has CLAUDE.md reading head, adds .claude/settings.json reading head-settings and deletes .mcp.json.
